1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,836
Wet clay hits a wall, and sticks.

2
00:00:02,836 --> 00:00:06,337
Two railway coaches couple
up, and roll away as one.

3
00:00:06,737 --> 00:00:08,622
In each crash, the bodies join.

4
00:00:08,622 --> 00:00:10,333
And something seems to vanish.

5
00:00:10,783 --> 00:00:14,305
In the college lab, Aarav rolls
a trolley into a still one.

6
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:15,881
Sticky pads on the front.

7
00:00:15,881 --> 00:00:17,090
They lock together.

8
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:20,534
Same mass, so the pair
rolls at half the speed.

9
00:00:20,534 --> 00:00:21,735
Momentum is fine.

10
00:00:21,735 --> 00:00:24,051
But half the kinetic energy is gone.

11
00:00:24,051 --> 00:00:25,260
Where did it go?

12
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,546
Let's find out, and
measure exactly how much.

13
00:00:29,146 --> 00:00:33,498
When two bodies stick together after
a hit, and move as one, it is called

14
00:00:33,498 --> 00:00:35,393
a perfectly inelastic collision.

15
00:00:35,743 --> 00:00:37,354
Momentum is still kept.

16
00:00:37,354 --> 00:00:39,771
The pushes between them are internal.

17
00:00:40,171 --> 00:00:42,407
But kinetic energy is not kept.

18
00:00:42,407 --> 00:00:45,875
Some of it turns into
heat, sound and bent pads.

19
00:00:46,475 --> 00:00:47,873
Our motion notebook.

20
00:00:47,873 --> 00:00:51,639
Trolley A, one kilogram, rolls
at six metres per second.

21
00:00:51,639 --> 00:00:54,446
Trolley B, two kilograms, waits at rest.

22
00:00:54,796 --> 00:00:56,333
They hit, and lock.

23
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:00,445
Now one body of three kilograms
rolls at two metres per second.

24
00:01:00,845 --> 00:01:02,409
Momentum: six before.

25
00:01:02,409 --> 00:01:04,390
Three times two, six after.

26
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:05,290
Kept.

27
00:01:05,344 --> 00:01:07,979
Kinetic energy: eighteen joules before.

28
00:01:07,979 --> 00:01:09,175
Only six after.

29
00:01:09,175 --> 00:01:10,573
Twelve joules lost.

30
00:01:10,573 --> 00:01:14,272
On the graph, the total
drops, and never comes back.

31
00:01:14,772 --> 00:01:15,689
Slow-mo replay.

32
00:01:15,689 --> 00:01:17,763
Freeze in the middle of the crunch.

33
00:01:18,113 --> 00:01:19,695
The pads are squashed.

34
00:01:19,695 --> 00:01:24,053
The pushes are equal and opposite,
so momentum moves from A to B.

35
00:01:24,453 --> 00:01:26,368
But the pads do not spring back.

36
00:01:26,368 --> 00:01:28,225
That stored energy never returns.

37
00:01:28,225 --> 00:01:30,528
It warms the pads, and makes the bang.

38
00:01:31,128 --> 00:01:32,269
Now swap them.

39
00:01:32,269 --> 00:01:36,005
Two kilograms rolls at six
into the one kilogram trolley.

40
00:01:36,005 --> 00:01:38,499
Will more energy be lost, or less?

41
00:01:38,499 --> 00:01:39,792
Pause and decide.

42
00:01:42,892 --> 00:01:43,792
Less!

43
00:01:43,428 --> 00:01:44,960
They roll on at four.

44
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:47,804
Thirty six joules before,
twenty four after.

45
00:01:47,804 --> 00:01:49,767
Only twelve lost, one third.

46
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:52,240
So the loss depends on which one moves.

47
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,638
Now the formulas, one step at a time.

48
00:01:54,988 --> 00:01:55,928
Step one.

49
00:01:55,928 --> 00:01:58,735
Momentum before equals momentum after.

50
00:01:58,735 --> 00:02:03,856
m one u one plus m two u two
equals m one plus m two, times v.

51
00:02:04,606 --> 00:02:05,506
Step two.

52
00:02:05,478 --> 00:02:10,521
So the common velocity v is the total
momentum divided by the total mass.

53
00:02:11,271 --> 00:02:12,232
Step three.

54
00:02:12,232 --> 00:02:16,523
Kinetic energy lost is the energy
before minus the energy after.

55
00:02:17,273 --> 00:02:18,246
Step four.

56
00:02:18,246 --> 00:02:20,091
Put v in and simplify.

57
00:02:20,091 --> 00:02:25,492
The loss is half, times m one m two
over m one plus m two, times u one

58
00:02:25,492 --> 00:02:27,325
minus u two, squared.

59
00:02:28,075 --> 00:02:29,209
Check run one.

60
00:02:29,209 --> 00:02:32,137
Half, times two thirds, times thirty six.

61
00:02:32,137 --> 00:02:33,210
Twelve joules.

62
00:02:33,810 --> 00:02:34,806
Remember this.

63
00:02:34,806 --> 00:02:39,292
When bodies stick together, momentum
is kept, but kinetic energy is lost.

64
00:02:39,992 --> 00:02:42,001
But why must energy be lost?

65
00:02:42,001 --> 00:02:43,080
Link by link.

66
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:46,994
Kinetic energy can be written
as p squared over two m.

67
00:02:47,394 --> 00:02:50,299
In the crash, the
momentum p stays the same.

68
00:02:50,699 --> 00:02:54,420
But after sticking, that same
p is carried by a bigger mass.

69
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:57,082
Same p on top, bigger m below.

70
00:02:57,082 --> 00:02:59,692
So the kinetic energy must get smaller.

71
00:03:00,292 --> 00:03:01,429
Side by side.

72
00:03:01,429 --> 00:03:02,881
Two kilograms each.

73
00:03:02,881 --> 00:03:06,028
One at six metres per second, one at rest.

74
00:03:06,428 --> 00:03:07,823
Elastic: they swap.

75
00:03:07,823 --> 00:03:08,841
Zero and six.

76
00:03:08,841 --> 00:03:10,632
All thirty six joules kept.

77
00:03:11,032 --> 00:03:14,303
Perfectly inelastic: they
stick, and roll at three.

78
00:03:14,303 --> 00:03:16,606
Eighteen joules kept, eighteen lost.

79
00:03:16,606 --> 00:03:19,511
That is the biggest loss
a collision can have.

80
00:03:20,111 --> 00:03:21,084
Now you try.

81
00:03:21,084 --> 00:03:24,931
Two equal trolleys at the same
speed hit head on, and stick.

82
00:03:24,931 --> 00:03:27,699
What fraction of the
kinetic energy is lost?

83
00:03:27,699 --> 00:03:28,909
Pause and decide.

84
00:03:32,109 --> 00:03:33,022
All of it!

85
00:03:33,022 --> 00:03:36,910
Their momenta are equal and
opposite, so the total is zero.

86
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:38,373
The pair stops dead.

87
00:03:39,023 --> 00:03:40,714
Now, one worked example.

88
00:03:41,064 --> 00:03:45,487
Fifty grams of putty at twenty metres
per second hits a nine hundred and

89
00:03:45,487 --> 00:03:48,166
fifty gram trolley at rest, and sticks.

90
00:03:48,166 --> 00:03:50,550
Find the speed and the energy lost.

91
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:54,684
Momentum before: zero point
zero five times twenty.

92
00:03:54,684 --> 00:03:56,888
One kilogram metre per second.

93
00:03:57,638 --> 00:04:00,096
The total mass is one kilogram.

94
00:04:00,096 --> 00:04:02,508
So v is one metre per second.

95
00:04:03,258 --> 00:04:07,977
Energy before: half, times zero point
zero five, times twenty squared.

96
00:04:07,977 --> 00:04:08,899
Ten joules.

97
00:04:08,899 --> 00:04:10,492
After: half a joule.

98
00:04:11,242 --> 00:04:13,723
So nine point five joules are lost.

99
00:04:13,723 --> 00:04:15,189
Ninety five percent!

100
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:17,303
Now, the exam trap.

101
00:04:17,653 --> 00:04:21,944
Many students think perfectly inelastic
means all the kinetic energy is

102
00:04:21,944 --> 00:04:22,844
lost.

103
00:04:22,909 --> 00:04:23,809
No.

104
00:04:23,329 --> 00:04:26,763
Only the share needed to make
them move together is lost.

105
00:04:26,763 --> 00:04:29,676
In run one, six of the
eighteen joules stayed.

106
00:04:30,326 --> 00:04:31,646
Where is this asked?

107
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:36,005
In numericals on common velocity, energy
lost, and bullets stuck in blocks.

108
00:04:36,605 --> 00:04:37,771
Exam level now.

109
00:04:37,771 --> 00:04:42,158
A twenty gram bullet at five hundred
metres per second sticks in a four

110
00:04:42,158 --> 00:04:44,737
point nine eight kilogram hanging block.

111
00:04:44,737 --> 00:04:45,637
g is ten.

112
00:04:45,606 --> 00:04:47,691
How high does the block swing?

113
00:04:47,691 --> 00:04:48,906
Pause and solve.

114
00:04:54,306 --> 00:04:55,446
The answer is B.

115
00:04:55,446 --> 00:04:56,612
Twenty centimetres.

116
00:04:57,112 --> 00:04:59,078
Momentum is kept in the hit.

117
00:04:59,078 --> 00:05:02,101
Zero point zero two times
five hundred is ten.

118
00:05:02,601 --> 00:05:07,002
The total mass is five kilograms, so
the block starts at two metres per

119
00:05:07,002 --> 00:05:07,902
second.

120
00:05:08,142 --> 00:05:10,517
Then energy is kept in the swing.

121
00:05:10,517 --> 00:05:12,534
h is v squared over two g.

122
00:05:12,534 --> 00:05:13,844
Four over twenty.

123
00:05:13,844 --> 00:05:15,471
Zero point two metres.

124
00:05:16,071 --> 00:05:17,612
Here is your recap.

125
00:05:17,612 --> 00:05:19,196
Screenshot this card.

126
00:05:22,396 --> 00:05:24,335
Can you answer these without help?

127
00:05:24,735 --> 00:05:25,635
One.

128
00:05:25,188 --> 00:05:28,200
Why do two trolleys that
stick together roll slower?

129
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,000
Two.

130
00:05:29,515 --> 00:05:31,603
Where does the lost kinetic energy go?

131
00:05:32,503 --> 00:05:33,403
Three.

132
00:05:33,048 --> 00:05:36,684
Two equal trolleys hit head on
at the same speed, and stick.

133
00:05:36,684 --> 00:05:37,595
What happens?

134
00:05:38,495 --> 00:05:42,610
Next time: three balls dropped on
the floor bounce to three heights.

135
00:05:42,610 --> 00:05:43,510
Why?

136
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,719
Coefficient of restitution.
